            <h3 class="headline">
                <span>Kantu for Chrome is a modern Selenium IDE plus additional features, open-source</span>
            </h3>
        </div> 

        <div class="span12">
            <p>
                Record and replay web macros with this  <span class="hired">free and open-source Chrome extension</span> for web browser automation. The extension is an easy to use web macro recorder for web developers, web testers
                and especially for general web automation and form filling.
            </p>
            <h2 id="video">Getting started with the Kantu Selenium IDE</h2>

            <iframe width="560" height="315" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/w6L5fs3Pyjo" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen></iframe>

            <p>
                This short screencast demos how to automate form filling and web testing with Kantu.
                We record the macro,  insert a PAUSE (3 seconds) command manually and then replay the macro twice.
            </p>

            <h2>Your next steps to become a web automation expert:</h2>
            <p>
                <ul class="list-group">
                    <li><i class="fa fa-newspaper-o"></i> <a href="/kantu/docs/webextensions">Kantu User Manual</a> - all features explained</li>
                    <li><i class="fa fa-laptop"></i> <a href="/kantu/docs/webextensions/selenium-ide/">Selenium IDE commands</a> - all supported commands, with examples</li>
                    <li><i class="fa fa-envelope"></i> Contact us: <a href="/contact">team AT a9t9.com</a> or <a href="https://github.com/A9T9/Kantu-for-Chrome">open a ticket</a>.</li>
                </ul>

            <p>
                <span class="hired">Need a specific feature added</span>, is your favorite Selenium IDE command still missing, or is your most annoying bug still not fixed?
                => <a href="/contact">Let us know!</a> We can only add features and fix bugs that are reported to us.

            </p>
 

            <a href="#start" style="float:right">Top</a>

            <h2>New: Start macros (test cases) from the command line</h2>
            <p>With the latest release we added <span class="hired">command line support</span>. 
            You can now <a href="/kantu/docs/webextensions#cmd">start macros from the command line</a> (e. g. via <a href="/howto/taskscheduler">task scheduler</a>) and 
            add macro shortcuts to <a href="/kantu/docs/webextensions#bookmarks">Chrome's bookmark bar</a>:
            </p>
            <p>
                <a href="/kantu/docs/webextensions#bookmarks">
                    <img src="~/Content/Images/addbookmark.jpg"  alt="Add web macro shortcut to bookmarks bar" class="responsive-img">
                </a>
               </br>A macro shortcut "bookmark" automatically opens Kantu, runs the macro and then closes Kantu again.
</p>


           <h2 id="bkup">100% Privacy: Everything is stored locally</h2>

            <p>
                All macros and settings are stored locally on your machine in what is called technically <a href="/howto/view-local-storage">HTML5 local storage</a>.
                <em>Nothing</em> is copied or moved to the cloud.
                This also means that once you uninstall the Kantu extension, your test cases (macros) are gone. 
                Please use the <a href="/kantu/docs/webextensions#bkup">export and export all</a> features to create backups of your
                important macros and  test suites. By default, Kantu prompts you every seven days to do a backup. 
            </p>

